Algorithm 1: QueryAgent   
1: Input: question $Q$ entity linking result $E$ instruction I, maximum iteration times $T$ 2: $t\gets 1$ .   
3: prompt $\leftarrow I + Q + E$ 4: $RM\gets \emptyset$ // Reasoning Memory   
5: while $t\leq T$ do   
6: thought, action $\leftarrow$ LLM(prompt);   
7: KB_fbPython_fb $\leftarrow$ Execute(action);   
8: current_info $\leftarrow$ Get Info in_This_Step();   
9: $RM\gets RM\cup$ current_info;   
10: env_fb $\leftarrow \{kb\_ fb,py\_ fb,RM\}$ .   
11: error $\leftarrow$ Detect_and_Distinguish_Err(env(fb);   
12: if error then   
13: guideline $\leftarrow$ Get_Guideline(error);   
14: obs $\leftarrow$ guideline;   
15: $RM\gets RM - \{\mathrm{current\_info}\}$ .   
16: else   
17: execution_result $\leftarrow$ kb_fb   
18: obs $\leftarrow$ execution_result;   
19: end if   
20: prompt $\leftarrow$ prompt $^+$ thought $^+$ action $^+$ observation;   
21: if action $=$ execute() then   
22: break;   
23: end if   
24: $t\gets t + 1$ .   
25: end while   
26: return execution_result;

# B.2 Detail Elaboration of Guidelines

In QueryAgent, the guidelines are served as the observation in our ReAct (Yao et al., 2023) style Agent. The content of the guideline depends on the

situation.

- When an error arises, the guideline is the description of what abnormal conditions occur and some possible solutions. For example, the guideline A, B, C,... in Figure 2. In this case, the LLM is conducting self-correction.   
